  "input": {
    "rationale": "Final status, no new records. Both investigations are complete, and with the two-voter vote repeat cited every case in either account now has at least two executions from retained inputs. Configuration recovery (98ee8dfd5fac4b84915f91ed4b094bcf-question-0, violated, defect asserted) cites eight receipts: single-voter recovery with flag-off controls (9a373c13...), the three-voter commit-rule witness (79a9cc34..., reproduced in four receipts), the durable-snapshot corruption surviving a flag-off restart (c477da09...), the authority pair with its premise-failure repeat and premise-enforcing revision (4178d9d5..., fe822d82..., 67fc59b5...), and the two-voter vote boundary in two executions (b9992882..., 0abdaee6...). Replay completion (29e4214f5ee146b393957fa23a33a73d-question-0, violated, defect asserted) cites eleven receipts across the block pair, the measured bound pair (e82594cc..., 962196ed...), the availability consequence at two batch sizes (ebb3bb9f..., fe822d82..., 67fc59b5..., 7ac7e4f6...), the exact 128-delivered-batch boundary at two batch sizes (8a710c75..., 9039d268..., f394d835...) and default-configuration reachability (0cb30b6b..., 9039d268...). A consistency check of 54 claims across 14 receipts found no discrepancy; both knowledge corrections raised by this evidence are recorded with affected uses marked and gaps answered. Remaining limits are structural (in-memory transports and stores in one process, no production store, no process-level restart or disk fault, one prefix shape per scenario, and the snapshot-shipping propagation path unexercised). The allocation is nearly exhausted and no probe that could not be cited is started; expiry preserves this state, with the two defects stated in the Interpretation records of their investigations.",
